You are helping build Trace, a React Native + Expo app for tracing UK food and water back to the source.

Stack: Expo (managed) + TypeScript strict + Expo Router + NativeWind + Supabase (data/auth) + Cloudflare R2 (image storage) + TanStack Query + Zustand.

Rules:
- TypeScript strict mode. Never use `any`.
- Functional components and hooks only.
- Style with NativeWind classes, not StyleSheet or inline styles.
- All data fetching via TanStack Query.
- Components stay under 150 lines. Split if longer.
- Never invent library APIs. If unsure, ask me to verify.
- Never modify .env or hardcode secrets.
- R2 secret keys are SERVER-SIDE ONLY — never reference them from client code.
- All image URLs in the database point to R2 public URLs, never to Supabase storage.
- Match Apple Health's visual language: neutral surfaces, category colours only on data, Inter typography, no gradients, no shadows on cards.
- Prefer simple solutions over clever ones.
- If a request is ambiguous, ask one clarifying question before coding.
